    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A **gerund** on its own can be a **command**, especially to **start moving** or speed up."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Common verbs: **andar, caminar, circular, salir, correr, moverse**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Firmer version: **estar** or **ir** + gerund in the present: **¡Ya te estás callando!** (_You'd better be quiet!_), **¡Te me vas saliendo!**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**¡Marchando!** is what a waiter calls when an order is on its way."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the gerund is already in motion, so it pushes people to move."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Vamos, ==saliendo== todos despacio y en silencio.",
              "en": "Come on, everyone out slowly and quietly."
            },
            {
              "es": "Ya son las tres. ¡==Andando==, que llegamos tarde!",
              "en": "It's three already. Let's go, we're going to be late!"
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Circulando==! Solo fue un choquecito.",
              "en": "Keep moving! It was just a fender bender."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Corriendo==, que nos mojamos!",
              "en": "Run, we're getting wet!"
            },
            {
              "es": "¡Ya te ==estás callando==!",
              "en": "You'd better be quiet right now!"
            }
          ]
        }
